Title: Restore the pre-Chrome-Refresh-2023 menu look
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo), ported from Thorium
Upstream-Source: electron-migrate/thorium-2024-ui-core.patch

Chrome Refresh 2023 made menus large, round and widely spaced. That reads as
native on macOS and as nothing at all on Windows, least of all Windows 7 and 8,
where Electron apps are claiming to draw native menus. This restores the older
metrics.

Ported from Thorium rather than copied. Three differences, all deliberate:

  * Unconditional, where Thorium gates everything on features::IsThorium2024().
    The flag exists so Thorium can ship both looks; this build only wants one,
    and carrying it would mean porting Thorium's ui_base_features hunks as well
    for a switch nobody here would flip.

  * Only the ui/ side -- see the end of this header for what was left out and
    why.

  * Restructured for Chromium 152. Thorium's GetCornerRadiusMetric switch reads
    ShapeContextTokens directly; upstream now maps context tokens to
    ShapeSysTokens first and switches on those, so the override moved to the top
    of the function. It is also deliberately non-exhaustive, where Thorium's is
    exhaustive with a NOTREACHED: anything unlisted falls through to upstream's
    mapping, so a token added by a future roll keeps working.

What each file does:

  ui/views/layout/layout_provider.cc
                          the pre-Refresh corner radii. kMenuRadius and
                          kMenuAuxRadius go to zero, which is the change that
                          actually squares the menus off -- MenuConfig's
                          corner_radius and auxiliary_corner_radius are
                          initialised from those tokens (see menu_config.h), so
                          everything else follows. kMenuTouchRadius stays
                          rounded at 8 rather than upstream's 12, as touch menus
                          should be. The rest (badge, textfield, button,
                          combobox, dialog, find bar, extensions menu button,
                          omnibox, content separator) take Thorium's values.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config.cc
                          the cross-platform metrics in InitCommon(): tighter
                          item margins and separators, no item horizontal
                          border padding, and an outer border. Upstream's value
                          is in a comment beside each one so the diff stays
                          readable as a set of deltas.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_config_win.cc
                          the Windows metrics, split on version. Windows 11
                          draws rounded menus natively, so it keeps a small
                          radius and the Refresh-era paddings; everything older
                          gets the classic square menu. use_bubble_border keys
                          off corner_radius, so the older path turns the bubble
                          border off by itself.

  ui/views/controls/menu/menu_item_view.cc
                          the classic triangular submenu arrow instead of the
                          Refresh chevron. components/vector_icons already
                          ships submenu_arrow_old.icon and lists it in its
                          BUILD.gn, so no resource work was needed.

Left out of Thorium's 57 files, having checked rather than assumed:

  chrome/browser/** (38)  UI Electron does not compile. The only
                          chrome/browser/ui/views/ sources chromium_src builds
                          are eye_dropper, the Picture-in-Picture overlay
                          controls, and the Linux status-icon and dark-mode
                          helpers.

  toggle_button, combobox, editable_combobox, tree_view
                          Electron's shell/ contains no views::ToggleButton,
                          views::Combobox, views::TreeView, views::Textfield or
                          views::DialogDelegate, and none of the chrome/ sources
                          above are those widgets. The corner-radius tokens for
                          them are taken anyway, since they cost one hunk in a
                          file this patch already touches.

  ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/** (3 CSS)
                          Electron does serve WebUI, but only two hosts:
                          chrome://devtools, whose front end carries its own
                          styling, and chrome://accessibility, whose resources
                          (chrome/browser/resources/accessibility/) are plain
                          CSS with no cr_elements, cr-button, cr-toggle or
                          md-select. The cr_elements targets are in Electron's
                          link graph, so the resources ship in the pak -- they
                          are simply never rendered. Note this does not affect
                          <select> in app content either: md_select_lit.css
                          styles chrome:// pages, and web-content select popups
                          are painted by Blink, not views.

  the three DISTANCE_* metrics
                          DISTANCE_TEXTFIELD_HORIZONTAL_TEXT_PADDING and
                          DISTANCE_CONTROL_VERTICAL_TEXT_PADDING need a views
                          Textfield or control, and DISTANCE_CLOSE_BUTTON_MARGIN
                          a views bubble close button. Of the compiled chrome/
                          sources, the only one reading LayoutProvider metrics
                          is overlay_window_live_caption_dialog.cc, which
                          chromium_src does not build.

  ui/base/ui_base_features.*, ui/resources/ui_resources.grd
                          the Thorium2024 flag and its resources; see above.

Verified by building ui/views:views. The look itself is unverified -- it needs
eyes on a real menu, which is also the only way to judge the metrics.

